N|               photo, and the name "CARLOS MORENO."
O|
N,G|               MED. SHOT -- REGGIE AND GRANDPIERRE
O|
C|                                     GRANDPIERRE
U|                         Have you nothing to say, Madame?
O|
N|               REGGIE looks down at the four passports, then back to 
N|               GRANDPIERRE.
O|
C|                                     REGGIE
P|                              (hopefully)
U|                         It's all right if you want to smoke 
U|                         your cigar now.
O|
S|               INT. LAMPERT APARTMENT -- DUSK
O|
N|               The house is empty as before. Now it is silent, the late 
N|               afternoon light coming from outside. REGGIE stands by a 
N|               window. A canvas airline bag rests on the floor nearby.
O|
N|               Suddenly there is the noise of a DOOR OPENING.
O|
N,G|               CLOSER SHOT -- REGGIE
O|
N|               As her head turns, in alarm, toward the noise. There is a 
N|               moment of silence, then FOOTSTEPS are heard, coming closer.
O|
N,G|               ANOTHER ANGLE
O|
N|               As PETER enters.
O|
C|                                     REGGIE
P|                              (surprised)
U|                         What are you doing here?
O|
C|                                     PETER
U|                         I phoned but nobody answered. I wanted 
U|                         to tell you how sorry I am -- and to 
U|                         find out if there was anything I 
U|                         could do.
O|
C|                                     REGGIE
U|                         How did you find out?
O|
C|                                     PETER
U|                         It's in all the afternoon papers. 
U|                         I'm very sorry.
O|
C|                                     REGGIE
U|                         Thank you.
O|
N|               A silence.
O|
C|                                     PETER
U|                         I rang the bell but I don't think 
U|                         it's working.
O|
C|                                     REGGIE
U|                         Yes it is -- I heard it this morning.
O|
N|               He looks around for the light switch, then goes to it and 
N|               flicks it on -- nothing happens. He flicks it a few more 
N|               times.
O|
C|                                     REGGIE
U|                         They must have turned off the 
U|                         electricity.
O|
N|               She shakes her head. PETER looks around.
O|
C|                                     PETER
U|                         Where did everything go?
O|
C|                                     REGGIE
U|                         Charles sold it all -- at auction.
O|
C|                                     PETER
U|                         Do you know what you're going to do?
O|
C|                                     REGGIE
