U|                         I suppose.
O|
C|                                     PETER
U|                         Doing what?
O|
C|                                     REGGIE
U|                         I'm a simultaneous translator -- 
U|                         like Sylvie, only she's English to 
U|                         French -- I'm French to English. 
U|                         That's what I did before I married 
U|                         Charles. The police probably think I 
U|                         killed him.
O|
C|                                     PETER
U|                         Instant divorce you mean?
O|
C|                                     REGGIE
U|                         Something like that. But I'm sorry 
U|                         it ended like this -- tossed off a 
U|                         train like a sack of third-class 
U|                         mail.
O|
C|                                     PETER
P|                              (Taking her hand)
U|                         Come on. You can't stay here.
O|
C|                                     REGGIE
U|                         I don't know where to go.
O|
C|                                     PETER
U|                         We'll find you a hotel.
O|
C|                                     REGGIE
U|                         Not too expensive -- I'm not a lady 
U|                         of leisure anymore.
O|
C|                                     PETER
U|                         Something modest but clean -- and 
U|                         near enough to UNESCO so you can 
U|                         take a cab when it rains -- okay?
O|
