N|               DOOR opening interrupts them. They turn to look.
O|
N,G|               MED. SHOT -- CHAPEL DOOR
O|
N|               Again the figure of a MAN is outlined in silhouette against 
N,G|               the outside brightness. When he closes the door we can see 
N,G,I|               "TEX" PENTHOLLOW, a slim, rangy man with sandy-colored hair, 
N|               a weatherbeaten face, washed-out blue-eyes -- also in his 
N|               forties. He wears a velvet-corduroy suit, string tie and a 
N|               bright yellow flower in his lapel. A bulldurham tag hangs 
N|               from his outside breast pocket, dangling from its string.
O|
N,G|               He starts down the aisle toward the bier, CAMERA LEADING 
N,G|               him, and we notice his unsteady gait. He turns to look at 
N|               the others present.
O|
N,G|               TRAVELING SHOT -- TEX'S P.O.V.
O|
N,G|               MOVING down the aisle. GRANDPIERRE's face, then GIDEON's, 
N,G|               then REGGIE's and SYLVIE's -- all staring at CAMERA.
O|
