O|
C,E|                                     REGGIE'S VOICE (O.S.)
U|                         No.
O|
C,E|                                     BARTHOLOMEW'S VOICE (O.S.)
U|                         The last one, please.
O|
N,G|               The glass and CAMERA move to the fourth face -- a young 
N|               SCOBIE.
O|
C,E|                                     REGGIE'S VOICE (O.S.)
U|                         That's a face you don't forget -- he 
U|                         was there too --
O|
C,E|                                     BARTHOLOMEW'S VOICE (O.S.)
U|                         Herman Scobie. And you've never seen 
U|                         him before, either?
O|
C,E|                                     REGGIE'S VOICE (O.S.)
U|                         No, thank heaven.
O|
N,G|               MED. SHOT -- REGGIE AND BARTHOLOMEW
O|
C|                                     BARTHOLOMEW
P|                              (a pause, regarding 
P|                              her)
U|                         Mrs. Lampert, I'm afraid you're in a 
U|                         great deal of danger.
O|
C|                                     REGGIE
U|                         Danger? Why should I be in any danger?
O|
C|                                     BARTHOLOMEW
U|                         You're Charles Voss's wife -- now 
U|                         that he's dead you're their only 
U|                         lead.
O|
C|                                     REGGIE
U|                         Mr. Bartholomew -- if you're trying 
U|                         to frighten me you're doing a really 
U|                         first-rate job!
P|                              (she takes another 
P|                              sandwich)
O|
C|                                     BARTHOLOMEW
U|                         Please, do what we ask, Mrs. Lampert -- 
U|                         it's your only chance.
O|
C|                                     REGGIE
U|                         Gladly, only I don't know what you 
U|                         want! You haven't told me.
O|
C|                                     BARTHOLOMEW
U|                         Oh, haven't I? The money -- Mrs. 
U|                         Lampert -- the money. The $250,000 
U|                         Charles Voss received from the 
U|                         auction. Those three men want it, 
U|                         too -- they want it very badly.
O|
C|                                     REGGIE
U|                         But it's Charles's money, not theirs.
O|
C|                                     BARTHOLOMEW
P|                              (laughing)
U|                         Oh, Mrs. Lampert! I'd love to see 
U|                         you try and convince them of that!
P|                              (drying his eyes)
U|                         Oh, dear.
O|
C|                                     REGGIE
U|                         Then whose is it? His or theirs?
O|
C|                                     BARTHOLOMEW
U|                         Ours.
O|
C|                                     REGGIE
P|                              (she looks at him for 
P|                              a moment)
U|                         Oh, I see.
O|
C|                                     BARTHOLOMEW
U|                         And I'm afraid we want it back.
O|
C|                                     REGGIE
U|                         But I don't have it.
O|
C|                                     BARTHOLOMEW
U|                         That's impossible. You're the only 
U|                         one who could have it.
O|
C|                                     REGGIE
U|                         I'm sorry it's impossible. It's the 
U|                         truth.
O|
N|               BARTHOLOMEW is silent for a moment, thinking.
O|
C|                                     BARTHOLOMEW
U|                         I believe you.
O|
C|                                     REGGIE
U|                         Thanks very much.
O|
C|                                     BARTHOLOMEW
U|                         Oh, you've got the money all right -- 
U|                         you just don't know you've got it.
O|
C|                                     REGGIE
U|                         Mr. Bartholomew -- if I had a quarter 
U|                         of a million dollars, believe me, 
U|                         I'd know it.
O|
C|                                     BARTHOLOMEW
U|                         Nevertheless, Mrs Lampert -- you've 
U|                         got it.
O|
C|                                     REGGIE
U|                         You mean it's just lying around 
U|                         someplace -- all that cash?
O|
C|                                     BARTHOLOMEW
U|                         Or a safe deposit key, a certified 
U|                         check, a baggage claim -- you look 
U|                         for it, Mrs. Lampert -- I'm quite 
U|                         sure you'll find it.
O|
C|                                     REGGIE
U|                         But --
O|
C|                                     BARTHOLOMEW
U|                         Look for it, Mrs. Lampert -- look 
U|                         just as hard and as fast as you can. 
U|                         You may not have a great deal of 
U|                         time. Those men know you have it 
U|                         just as surely as we do. You won't 
U|                         be safe until the money's in our 
U|                         hands. Is that clear?
O|
N|               REGGIE nods. He writes something on a pad of paper and tears 
N|               it off, handing it to her.
O|
C|                                     BARTHOLOMEW
U|                         Here's where you're to call me -- 
U|                         day or night. It's a direct line to 
U|                         both my office and my apartment. 
U|                         Don't lose it, Mrs. Lampert -- and 
U|                         please don't tell anyone about coming 
U|                         to see me. It could prove fatal for 
U|                         them as well as yourself.
O|
C|                                     REGGIE
