S|               EXT. ESPLANADE DES CHAMPS-ELYÉES -- DAY
O|
N,G|               MED. SHOT -- GUIGNOL.
O|
N|               One of the French Punch and Judy shows set up on certain 
S|               days in the small park alongside the broad avenue between 
N|               the Rond Point and the Place de la Concorde. At the moment, 
N|               Judy, as always, is beating Punch with a bat. The sound of 
N|               CHILDREN laughing and screaming can be heard.
O|
N,G|               VARIOUS CLOSE SHOTS -- THE CHILDREN
O|
N|               Sitting on small benches lined up to face the stage. Their 
N|               attention is fixed on the show, their belief totally suspended 
N|               by the play as only children's can be -- laughing at the 
N|               slapstick, booing the villain, frightened by the perils.
O|
N,G|               MED. SHOT -- REGGIE
O|
N|               Sitting on the last bench, next to some CHILDREN. They are 
N|               laughing but she isn't -- she just watches, her attention 
N|               caught up but her face void of emotion. The bench is too low 
N|               for her, forcing her knees up almost under her chin.
O|
N|               After a moment, PETER comes up behind her and, stepping over 
N|               the benches, sits beside her. She doesn't seem to notice.
O|
N|               [Throughout the following scene the CHILDREN and the ACTORS 
N|               can be heard in the b.g.]
O|
C|                                     PETER
U|                         Reggie -- ?
O|
N|               She turns and looks at him for a moment.
O|
C|                                     REGGIE
P|                              (vaguely)
U|                         Hallo, Peter.
O|
C|                                     PETER
U|                         You telephoned me to meet you. I've 
U|                         been standing on the corner back 
U|                         there -- waiting for you.
O|
C|                                     REGGIE
U|                         I'm sorry -- I heard the children 
U|                         laughing.
O|
N|               A ROAR from the CHILDREN. REGGIE and PETER turn toward the 
N|               stage.
O|
N,G|               MED. SHOT -- GUIGNOL
O|
N|               PUNCH and JUDY are arguing loudly.
O|
N,G|               TWO SHOT -- REGGIE AND PETER
O|
C|                                     PETER
U|                         What's going on?
O|
C|                                     REGGIE
U|                         Don't you understand French?
O|
C|                                     PETER
U|                         I'm still having trouble with English.
O|
C|                                     REGGIE
