S|               REVERSE SHOT -- 'PHONE BOOTH -- NIGHT
O|
N|               TEX PENTHOLLOW, the second man from the funeral (and photo), 
N|               the man in the corduroy suit and string tie, stands in the 
N|               doorway, his face calm, a hand-rolled but unlit cigarette in 
N|               his mouth. He has put one foot up against the side of the 
N|               door so she can't leave. REGGIE stares at him, terrified.
O|
C|                                     TEX
U|                         Howdy, Miz Lampert.
O|
C|                                     REGGIE
U|                         Wha -- what do you want?
O|
N|               TEX takes a book of matches from his pocket.
O|
C|                                     TEX
U|                         You know what I want, Miz Lampert...
O|
C|                                     REGGIE
U|                         No -- no, I'm don't.
O|
C|                                     TEX
U|                         Come on now -- sure you do. An' you'd 
U|                         better give it to me, Miz Lampert -- 
U|                         cuz I ain't foolin'. No sireebob!
O|
N|               He strikes a match and lights his cigarette, holding the 
N|               burning match in his hand afterward.
O|
C|                                     REGGIE
U|                         I don't know what --
