O|
N|               REGGIE comes out of the shadows, looks after DYLE's taxi, 
N|               then hails another one which pulls up.
O|
C|                                     REGGIE
P|                              (to DRIVER)
U|                         Aux Halles -- vite!
O|
D|               DELETED
O|
S|               EXT. LES HALLES -- NIGHT
O|
N|               REGGIE and BARTHOLOMEW walking. The Central Market is teeming 
N|               with activity -- trucks creeping around other trucks, cases 
N|               of fruit and vegetables stacked on every inch of sidewalk, 
N|               WORKERS of all types milling around, unloading trucks and 
N|               stacking crates, little electric carts scooting in and out -- 
N|               and nearby, one of the huge, high-roofed sheds where the 
N|               butchers work.
O|
N,G|               TWO SHOT -- REGGIE AND BARTHOLOMEW
O|
N,G|               CAMERA LEADING them as they walk.
O|
C|                                     BARTHOLOMEW
P|                              (looking around)
U|                         Incredible, isn't it? Zola called it 
U|                         'le ventre de Paris' -- the womb of 
U|                         Paris, the belly.
O|
N|               She takes a banana from a nearby stall.
O|
C|                                     REGGIE
P|                              (peeling it)
U|                         What did you want to see me about, 
U|                         Mr. Bartholomew?
O|
C|                                     BARTHOLOMEW
P|                              (leaves a coin on the 
P|                              crate)
U|                         Were you followed?
O|
C|                                     REGGIE
U|                         Yes, but I lost him. I really did it 
U|                         quite brilliantly. I'm beginning to 
U|                         think women make the best spies.
O|
C|                                     BARTHOLOMEW
U|                         Agents.
O|
C|                                     REGGIE
U|                         He has a gun, Mr. Bartholomew -- I 
U|                         saw it.
O|
C|                                     BARTHOLOMEW
U|                         Who?
O|
C|                                     REGGIE
U|                         Dyle, or whatever his name is.
O|
C|                                     BARTHOLOMEW
U|                         What does your Mr. Dyle look like, 
U|                         Mrs. Lampert?
O|
C|                                     REGGIE
U|                         He's hardly my Mr. Dyle.
O|
C|                                     BARTHOLOMEW
U|                         Describe him.
O|
C|                                     REGGIE
U|                         Well -- he's tall -- over six feet -- 
U|                         rather thin -- in good physical shape, 
U|                         I'd say -- dark eyes -- quite 
U|                         handsome, really.
O|
C|                                     BARTHOLOMEW
P|                              (shaking his head)
U|                         No.
O|
C|                                     REGGIE
U|                         No, what?
O|
C|                                     BARTHOLOMEW
U|                         That's not Carson Dyle.
O|
C|                                     REGGIE
P|                              (stopping)
U|                         Carson?
O|
C|                                     BARTHOLOMEW
U|                         There's only one Dyle connected with 
U|                         this affair, Mrs. Lampert -- that's 
U|                         Carson.
O|
C|                                     REGGIE
