U|                         Besides, you said yourself, women 
U|                         make the best spies.
O|
C|                                     REGGIE
P|                              (resigned)
U|                         Agents.
O|
S|               EXT. HOTEL (PLACE ST. ANDRÉ DES ARTS) -- LATE AFTERNOON
O|
N|               DYLE leaves the hotel and turns into the Place. A moment 
N|               later, REGGIE comes cautiously from the hotel. As she watches 
N|               DYLE, a SANDWICH-MAN advertising a driving school passes the 
N|               hotel. REGGIE falls in behind him, his tall placard hiding 
N|               her from view.
O|
S|               EXT. PLACE ST. ANDRÉ DES ARTS -- LATE AFTERNOON
O|
N|               First comes DYLE, passing a sidewalk cafe on the corner, 
N|               then the SANDWICH-MAN and REGGIE. The SANDWICH-MAN turns 
N|               off, leaving REGGIE out in the open. A moment later, DYLE 
N|               passes a GIRL painting a canvas, her easel set up in the 
N|               middle of the sidewalk. He stops when he has passed her and 
N|               turns to look at her work. REGGIE, not knowing what to do, 
N|               and afraid she will be seen by DYLE, who is now looking her 
N|               way, spins and sits at the sidewalk cafe's nearest table, 
N|               her back to DYLE. It is already occupied by a middle-aged 
N|               TOURIST.
O|
N,G|               TWO SHOT -- REGGIE AND TOURIST
O|
N|               The TOURIST, complete with camera, beret and guide book, 
N|               looks up from his coffee, surprised. He stares at REGGIE and 
N|               she stares back. Finally, not knowing what else to do, she 
N|               smiles, then takes a portion of his brioche and eats it.
O|
N|               He smiles back emptily, not knowing what to make of her.
O|
N|               REGGIE turns to look at DYLE.
O|
N,G|               MED. SHOT -- DYLE
O|
N|               He has made his judgment of the painting and now moves on.
O|
N,G|               TWO SHOT -- REGGIE AND TOURIST
O|
N|               The TOURIST has finally found the courage to speak. As he 
N|               opens his mouth to make a sound, REGGIE, her eyes on DYLE, 
N|               rises quickly from the table and goes, leaving a very confused 
N|               TOURIST with his mouth open. He blinks, then leaves some 
N|               money on the table and starts after her.
O|
S|               EXT. PLACE ST. ANDRÉ DES ARTS -- LATE AFTERNOON
O|
