P|                              (after a pause)
U|                         That's a crock! If one of us did 
U|                         that he wouldn't hang around here 
U|                         waiting for the other two to wise 
U|                         up.
O|
C|                                     DYLE
U|                         But he'd have to. If he left he'd be 
U|                         admitting his guilt -- and the others 
U|                         would know what happened. Whoever it 
U|                         is has to wait here, pretending to 
U|                         look for the money, waiting for the 
U|                         rest of us to give up and go home. 
U|                         That's when he'll be safe and not a 
U|                         minute before.
O|
N|               A pause as the THREE MEN look at one another.
O|
C|                                     GIDEON
U|                         Up till now we always figured she 
U|                         had the money -- but you know so 
U|                         much about it, maybe you've got it.
O|
C|                                     DYLE
U|                         Then what am I doing here? You didn't 
U|                         know anything about me -- I'm the 
U|                         only one who could have taken it and 
U|                         kept right on going.
O|
C|                                     SCOBIE
U|                         He's just tryin' to throw us off! 
U|                         They've got it, I tell you! Why don't 
U|                         we search their rooms?
O|
C|                                     DYLE
P|                              (exchanging looks 
P|                              with REGGIE)
U|                         It's all right with us --
O|
C|                                     TEX
P|                              (rising)
U|                         What are we wastin' time for? Let's 
U|                         go.
O|
C|                                     DYLE
U|                         And while we're waiting, we might as 
U|                         well go through yours.
O|
C|                                     SCOBIE
P|                              (stopping)
U|                         Not my room!
O|
C|                                     DYLE
U|                         What's wrong, Herman -- have you got 
U|                         something to hide?
P|                              (a pause, then smiling)
U|                         Then I take it there are no 
U|                         objections.
O|
N|               The THREE MEN look at one another unhappily.
O|
C|                                     DYLE
U|                         We'd better exchange keys. Here's 
U|                         mine.
O|
C|                                     SCOBIE
U|                         I'll take that.
O|
N|               He takes DYLE's key and gives DYLE his. GIDEON goes to REGGIE, 
N|               takes her key and gives her his own.
O|
C|                                     TEX
U|                         Mine's in the door. Ariva durchy, 
U|                         y'all.
O|
N|               The THREE MEN file out. DYLE and REGGIE exchange looks.
O|
C|                                     DYLE
U|                         Come on -- let's get busy. Who gets 
U|                         your vote?
O|
C|                                     REGGIE
U|                         Scobie -- he's the one that objected.
O|
C|                                     DYLE
P|                              (handing her the boy)
U|                         He's all yours. I'll do Tex and 
U|                         Gideon. Take Jean-Louis with you -- 
U|                         and make sure you bolt the door from 
U|                         inside.
O|
C|                                     REGGIE
U|                         Viens, Jean-Louis -- we're going to 
U|                         have a treasure hunt.
O|
C|                                     JEAN-LOUIS
P|                              (joining them)
U|                         Oh, la! If I find the treasure, will 
U|                         I win a prize?
O|
C|                                     REGGIE
P|                              (to DYLE)
U|                         What should we give him?
O|
C|                                     DYLE
U|                         How about $25,000? Or do you think 
U|                         it would spoil him?
O|
N|               She smiles, takes JEAN-LOUIS' hand and leaves. DYLE turns to 
N|               survey TEX's room.
O|
N|               He goes first to the drawer in the night table -- empty; and 
N|               the bed, looking in it and under it. Then he goes to the 
N|               desk and opens the drawers -- also empty. The bureau is next -- 
N|               he opens all three double drawers and they, too, are 
N|               completely empty. Frowning, he goes to the armoire and opens 
N|               it -- shelves and hanging bar are likewise bare.
O|
N,G|               Then, CAMERA PANNING DOWN, he sees the only thing he's found 
N|               so far in the room -- a pair of fine cowboy boots.
O|
S|               INT. REGGIE'S ROOM -- NIGHT
O|
N,G|               CLOSE SHOT -- AIRLINES BAG. CAMERA PULLS BACK to include 
N|               GIDEON, staring down at it as it lies on the table in the 
N|               center of the room.
O|
C|                                     GIDEON
P|                              (eyes on the bag)
U|                         Tex?
O|
N,G|               ANOTHER ANGLE
O|
N,G|               Including TEX, busy going through the bureau. He looks up, 
N|               then joins GIDEON.
O|
C|                                     TEX
U|                         What's that?
O|
