N|               moving down again. GIDEON shakes his head and leans back, 
N|               whistling again. The cage comes to his floor and starts past 
N|               it. Seeing this, GIDEON looks confused.
O|
S|               INT. HOTEL LOBBY -- NIGHT
O|
N|               The NIGHT PORTER is asleep behind the desk. The elevator, 
N|               GIDEON inside, keeps coming down. It passes the lobby level 
N|               and keeps right on going, toward the basement.
O|
C|                                     GIDEON
U|                         Hey! How do you stop this thing?
O|
N|               The elevator passes out of sight, still going down. There is 
N|               a silence as the motor stops, and then a series of sneezes 
N|               that ends with a terrifying shriek. The NIGHT PORTER, rudely 
N|               awakened, runs to the elevator shaft, his shoes squeaking 
N|               horribly. He looks up, sees nothing, then looks down. He 
N|               presses the call button and the motor starts.
O|
N|               An instant later the cage appears and stops. The NIGHT PORTER 
N,G|               opens the gate, pulls back the grill and the CAMERA RUSHES 
N,G|               PAST him to pick up GIDEON. His body is sitting on the floor 
N|               of the cage, its grotesque sprawling attitude resembling a 
N|               puppet's with its strings cut. Except that GIDEON has no 
N|               strings to cut -- only a throat. From ear to ear.
O|
