C|                                     BRITISH DELEGATE
U|                         Mr. Chairman, fellow delegates -- my 
U|                         distinguished colleague from Italy. 
U|                         Her Majesty's delegation has listened 
U|                         with great patience to the Southern 
U|                         European position on this problem, 
U|                         and while we find it charmingly 
U|                         stated, we cannot possibly agree 
U|                         with its content. In 1937, in the 
U|                         British colonies of Kenya, Uganda 
U|                         and Tanganyika -- and, if I'm not 
U|                         mistaken, more or less in Somaliland -- 
U|                         a programme of crop rotation was 
U|                         instituted vis-à-vis arable land 
U|                         which had never before known the 
U|                         plough, beginning before the soil 
U|                         was able to know the sort of fatigue 
U|                         now plaguing most of Western Europe. 
U|                         In 1937, therefore, Her Majesty's 
U|                         Government -- at that time His 
U|                         Majesty's Government -- was able to 
U|                         properly assay the situation. We 
U|                         therefore oppose the resolution.
